<title>NETHERLANDS: Dutch grain crop forecast up in 1996.</title>
<headline>Dutch grain crop forecast up in 1996.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1996-11-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Dutch grain crop is forecast at 1.57 million tonnes in 1996 against 1.44 million in 1995, the Dutch statistical office said on Tuesday.  </p>
<p>The higher grain crop was attributed to a rise in yields per hectare and to an extension to the growing area.</p>
<p>The forecast covers the production of wheat, oats, barley and rye. Record production of winter wheat made up 1.22 million tonnes of the total grain crop from 1.10 million in 1995. --Amsterdam Newsroom +31 20 504 5000</p>
</text>
